//! edit.impl — the built-in implementations the registry's ONE invoke
//! matches on.
//!
//! The port's half of sagitta's `CmdDesc.fn` (`cmd.h:137-160`): each C
//! handler campaign 03 ports has an implementation id here, assigned in
//! the descriptor table's order; `impl_of_handler` maps C's handler name
//! (the generated table's second field) to it — two descriptors with one
//! handler share it, which is what makes an alias pair — and `run_impl`
//! is the `match` (the shape ruled at launch: no function value crosses
//! a module boundary, G19/G20, wolf-lang#806). Every other handler is
//! `IMPL_UNPORTED`, which refuses naming its sprint and lane
//! (`cmd_unported_message`).

/// A C handler campaign 03 has not ported.
pub const IMPL_UNPORTED: int = 1

